def dictionary(columns):
    missing = set(columns)-DESCRIPTIONS.keys()
    if missing:
        raise ValueError(f"Undocumented table columns: {sorted(missing)}")
    intro = """# Canonical analysis table

One row per version, instance, epsilon and arm/ablation. Blank CSV cells are null, never imputed zero.
All costs use sums of unsquared Euclidean distances and score assignments on original C.
Public selectors are derived operating points; their copied samples are not independent replications.
Keep the three frozen cube configurations separate. New geometry replicates permit a separate
between-dataset analysis; the reported Student-t intervals describe mechanism noise only.
The scaled Appendix family changes data when epsilon changes. Fixed-instance epsilon sweeps do not.
Noiseless proxy and exact-radius rows are NONPRIVATE DIAGNOSTICS, not private competitors.
Per-draw samples, source geometry, environment and public candidate scores live in immutable atomic checkpoints.
The source registry is used only when rebuilding this table, never for ordinary plotting.

| Column | Definition and units |
| --- | --- |
"""
    return intro + "".join(f"| `{name}` | {DESCRIPTIONS[name]} |\n" for name in columns)
